    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mid terrace, two bedroom home with excellent upgrade potential in a mature and central Drogheda location. The property qualifies for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant which makes it an ideal project for buyers looking to modernise and add value. The property has been stripped back to the shell, providing a blank canvas and a clear advantage for refurbishment. \n\nThe property enjoys an exceptionally large front and rear garden, not overlooked with generous off?street parking. commanding uninterrupted views over the River Boyne.\n\nAccommodation includes an open plan kitchen/living room, utility/downstairs WC, main bathroom and two double rooms.\n\nEasy access through a vehicular gate to the rear of the property via Mell Lane.\nLocated in a long established residential area, St. Joseph?s terrace is within walking distance of Drogheda town centre, local schools, shops, bus routes, and a range of amenities. \n\nAccess to the M1 north and south bound is also close by. The local M1 Retail park is anchored by Woodie?s DIY, Tesco and Lidl while Aldi is within a 5 minute walk. \n\nThis property represents a superb opportunity for buyers seeking a home they can transform to their own taste while availing of significant refurbishment supports or the property investor alike. No previous RTB registration and vacant possession allows for RPZ exemption allowing the discerning investor achieve full open market rent on completion. \n\nFeatures\nShort distance from Drogheda town centre\nAccess to M1 close by\nmature development\nGas fired central heating\nSecure rear entrance from Mell Lane\nQualifies for vacant property grant\nInvestment opportunity\nUninterrupted Boyne River Views\nHeld freehold\nExceptionally large gardens not overlooked\n\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nKitchen/living Room\nCast iron fireplace, marble hearth\n\n\nBathroom/utility\nRoom to the rear of the property with provisions for toilet and waste, exits onto rear of property\n\nMain bathroom\nTiled throughout, whb, toilet, electric shower\n\nBedroom 1\nBedroom 2\n\nConstruction\nThe property is of a typical concrete construction with a red brick outer leaf, double glazing, uPVC front and rear doors. uPVC fascia, soffit and downpipes. \n\nOutside\nEnclosed rear garden with concrete panelled boundary walls, rear access from Mell Lane.\nFront garden with off street parking.\n\n\nEssential services\nMains water\nMains sewerage\nProvisions for GFCH/mechanical fit out\nOff street parking\n\nViewing\nBy appointment only\n\nNegotiator\nAnthony Byrne\nAssocSCSI/AssocRICS\nH.Cert. Property Studies\nN.Dip. Building Surveying\nlicense no. 003939-007400\n\n\n"
      },
